{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/582548-micro-dark-era-counter-cultural-usa","id":582548,"title":"Micro Dark Era - Counter Cultural USA","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-07T11:37:56-07:00","id":582548,"title":"Micro Dark Era - Counter Cultural USA","content":"The countercultural revolution was a turbulent time for the vigil. A young generation eager to escape the stifling culture of their parents unearthed monsters and occult lore as they explored new scientific, philosophical and spiritual ideas. To historians of the Vigil, such that they are, the countercultural revolution is often seen as a continuation or final resurgence of The War. Once again powerful Conspiracies were shaken and new groups formed to fill the vacuum.<br /> <br /> If the stormy sixties were a continuation of The War than they were a continuation in more than spirit. The Shadow of World War II still loomed large over the Vigil. Without the destructions of many established Conspiracies during the War (and European Colonisation centuries before) the events of the decade simply could not have taken place. Ideas and discoveries that gave birth to Cells and Compacts in the 1960s would have been prevented or appropriated a few decades earlier by Conspiracies eager to protect their monopoly or destroy whatever foul monster a well meaning student might blunder into.<br /> <br /> Other historians say that the countercultural revolution was not a continuation. It was the pendulum swinging back towards the centre as a young generation explored new philosophical and spiritual ideas; bringing a sense of mysticism and a spirit of revolution to counterbalance the predominantly technological and government backed organisations born in the fires of World War II. Many of the groups were overtly political, with strong ties to civilian ideologies.<br /> <br /> Whether it was an echo or the returning pendulum; the stormy sixties were but a puff of air before the howling fury of The War, the alliances forged were mere Compacts compared to the grand Conspiracies backed by the might of empires that arose in previous decades. Indeed, by the decade's end most of them had been consumed by larger groups eager to plunder their knowledge, censor unAmerican activities, or assert their monopolies on certain areas of occult lore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Peace and Love For Sale</span><br /> <br /> The hippy movement preached peace, free love and returning to nature. In the world of Darkness any Shaman, Werewolf, or Vampire crone could tell you one of those three things was not like the others.<br /> <br /> Which is not to say the hippies were doomed by their ignorance. Some retreated back to the cities and never again attempted to reconnect with nature after a Werewolf pack firmly told them to get off their territory. Other hippies ended up recruited into werewolf packs or a shaman's following, which is not always a bad fate, or a Vampire's blood-and-nature cult, is pretty much always a bad thing.<br /> <br /> But not every hippy sold out to monsters or capitalism as soon as they realised their ideology was wrong about Mother Earth. Many returned safely from the wilderness, disillusioned about nature but still confident in the moral principles of the hippy movement. As they had accepted the existence of the supernatural they were Hunters, even if they did not actually Hunt anything. These Hunters lived among their fellow hippies, and when someone had an encounter with the supernatural they were there with a supportive ear.<br /> <br /> It was the presence of Hunters that allowed the hippy movement to develop a supernatural base of it's own. Hardcore psychonaughts were starting to uncover some very effective concoctions, as they peered into the Shadow on an acid trip or unlocked latent psychic abilities though mushrooms Hunters in the movement were there to gently suggest they accept what they saw no matter how easy it would be to write it off as a bad trip. As their products got more reliable (though not safer) a radical splinter of hippy hunters began to form. If nature was red in tooth and claw they would tame the spiritscape and create the green land of peace and free love they wanted.<br /> <br /> Towards the mid sixties dozens of communes were formed. Stocked heavily with spirit seeing drugs these communes began to create spiritual landscapes of peace and cooperation through, well just trial and error. And there was a lot of error. In some commune the presence of so many people trying for spiritual awareness weakened the Gauntlet allowing possessions and manifestations, in others attempts to nurture the right sort of spirits led to a feedback loop that overran the local spiritual ecosystem and the minds of any humans nearby. More than once hippies went back to the Werewolves or Shaman who'd disgusted them years ago to beg for help. Others were destroyed by enemies, usually Werewolves, who objected to mortals tampering with the spirit world.<br /> <br /> But most of the communes lasted for a while. A few even succeeded at their aims and the rest were simply yet another commune with an ineffectual occult communal works project. They survived until they met an enemy more powerful than any they had faced before. The Federal Drug Administration.<br /> <br /> Some say it was an operation by Task Force: VALKYRIE that was infiltrated by The Cheiron Group. Others say Cheiron was running the show and VALKYRIE were infiltrators. In the back channels of Network Zero there are claims that it was actually Last Dysterty International and rumours that the Russians or international drug runners were involved. Outside the upper echelons of the Conspiracies all that can be known for sure is that somebody pushed the FDA into a massive series of raids. Entire communes were arrested and drug labs burned; then during a media blackout the chemists, the most experienced psychonaughts, the psychics, in short anyone with valuable knowledge, just vanished into thin air.<br /> <br /> The last surviving communes, even a couple of successful spirit scapes, survived because they exclusively imported their drugs from other communes and because they got damn lucky. But cut off from their suppliers their days were numbered. Some continued their work blindly, attempting to manipulate a spirit ecology they could no longer see or measure. The rest advertised for a shaman to take over and lead the project in the hope that their past successes might attract someone who agreed with their ideals. Most simply gave up, and the dream of a home grown occult hippy movement creating a loving natural world died with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Feminine Mystics</span><br /> <br /> Feminism had less of an effect on the Vigil than one might expect. All Hunters ignore social conventions, starting with the one about pretending the supernatural doesn't exist, and many take it futher. If a millennia old Conspiracy such as the Ageis Kai Doru takes a contrarian position on gender essentialism the tutting neighbours are unlikely to notice and would be unable to do much if they did.<br /> <br /> The actual connection between the feminist movement and the Vigil is a little more indirect, forming through related areas like archeology, literature criticism, and neo-paganism. Attempts to create a new mythology that understands and exults the feminine perspective. Most of these projects had no interest in genuine occult lore, and those that did showed the typical accuracy of a rookie hunter with no institutional knowledge to draw upon, which is to say they were near universally wrong on all accounts.<br /> <br /> But it is a willingness to explore beyond social conventions that leads one to the supernatural, accuracy has nothing to do with it. During the decade there were several notable encounters between feminists and the supernatural that forged a solid, if short lived, connection between feminism and the Vigil.<br /> <br /> The largest single point of contact came through Wiccia, and to a lesser extent other neo-pagan faiths. By the 1960s Wiccians had undertaken fifteen years of enthusiastic occult investigations during the turbulent, and thus fruitful, war and postwar periods. In addition to their own modest discoveries many covens had attracted patronage from a sometimes benevolent witch or ghostwalker, or a rarely benevolent vampire curious to see if there was any substance to wiccian \u201cwitchcraft\u201d. By the time the first public Dianic Wiccian coven was officially formed in 1971 neo-pagan influenced Cells dedicated to fighting or learning from the supernatural had been growing within the feminist movement for years.<br /> <br /> When their exposure from the supernatural didn't come from neo-paganism it came from the abundance of low hanging fruit during the countercultural period. Just a few decades earlier several Conspiracies were destroyed, their lore and occult tomes were scattered, and often left where a student critiquing classical mythology for her thesis could stumble upon it. Archeological sites that were once quietly guarded now offered their secrets freely. For feminist students, indeed for any students, it was either the best or worst time to be interested in myths.<br /> <br /> [picture: An archeologist holds something that looks like Venus of Willendorf, she screams in pain from contact with the supernatural object. If you play Darkest Dungeon, the Vestel's affliction animation would be a good model]<br /> <br /> Almost from the beginning the burgeoning feminist hunter community had a strained relationship with the regular feminist community. It is far harder to reinterpret a text on the worship of an ancient goddess through a feminist lens when your patron is a witch who'll tell you if your interpretation makes theurgy more or less effective (neo-pagans, incidentally, dealt with similar problems a decade ago by mostly deciding they didn't mind what regular society thought).<br /> <br /> This ideological turmoil would simmer through the Cells and occasional Compacts for the duration of the countercultural revolution, many feminist hunters found themselves returning to academia or activism after a short Vigil. Others found that building their Vigil atop a shaky ideological foundation made them easy recruits for established hunter societies, or worse. By the end of the countercultural period, when Conspiracies began to absorb or squash the newer societies, there was scarcely anyone left to resist them.<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar: Survivors</b><br /> <br /> Not all the feminist organisations born during the countercultural period were destroyed, assimilated or faded away. Among the successful survivors are the Maiden's Blood Sisterhood and the Athenic Church.<br /> <br /> The Sisterhood, who might be more accurately described as a compact full of feminists rather than a feminist compact, adopted a fairly typical goal of protecting humans from monsters. Their straightforward mission shielded them from ideological turmoil while their tendency to recruit from respectable upper class families and for their alumni to take positions at more powerful Conspiracies gave them protection from the backlashes at the end of the countercultural period.<br /> <br /> As for the Athenic Church, they share some responsibility for why so few feminist Compacts survived beyond the countercultural period. Their flashy and impressive blessings enabled the Church to poach members, and mount the occasional crusade, against feminist and neo-pagan organisations. Even hunters who weren't directly affected often found the Church's actions disillusioning. The publication of When God Was a Woman in 1976 is generally understood as the moment when feminist hunters abandoned all attempts of reconciling their personal experiences with mainstream feminism theory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">The Man is Sucking Me Dry</span><br /> <br /> For almost as long as the student protesters imagined some old white guy in a suit as The Man countercultural Hunters of all stripes and backgrounds were picturing The Man as a very white guy in an opera cape. To understand how Vampires became the prime evil for a generation of Hunters you must go back in time.<br /> <br /> Two decades before the summer of love Task Force: VALKYRIE had a problem, that problem was communism, and also Witches. The Task Force's increasing competence at getting information about Witches had unearthed a recent and growing vein of socialism. To say the Men in Black were terrified would be putting it mildly but between their regular monster hunting duties and Ivan VALKYRIE just didn't have the resources to open a third front, and so they made a Faustian bargain that still haunts them them to this day. They funded vampires to fight a proxy war against the witches.<br /> <br /> But to get the full story you must go back even earlier, to America's shameful history of slavery. Vampires are timeless creatures, and rather predictable in their way. They need blood, and slaves were an almost limitless supply. In turn the Cainite Heresy, who only see race as \u201chuman, vampire and everyone else\u201d, did as they always had done and recruited the vampire's victims, slaves and abolitionists alike.<br /> <br /> In the 1960s these two stories combined in a perfect storm that would define a generation of the American Vigil.<br /> <br /> By the time the countercultural era came around centuries of predation had created an enormous concentration of Canites among African Americans; a young, angry, heavily armed, black man in the 60s could be explain himself in one of two ways: Civil rights activist or vampire hunter. Unsurprisingly the Canites chose the former and quickly became vocal and well placed members of the civil rights movement; despite their unworkable vampire-centric theory of race relations.<br /> <br /> The Canites, or Hunters in general, embedding themselves in revolutionary movements is nothing new. The experienced Vampire knows when to fade away and let mortals figure it out, and that's just what would have happened if the experienced vampires hadn't been usurped two decades earlier by younger monsters with equipment, funding, and most importantly, cover ups courtesy of Uncle Sam. What's more, many of the new Vampire elite were slave owners in life and took the civil rights movement rather personally.<br /> <br /> And so the Canites dragged counterculture hunters into their conflict with vampires, the vampires brought in the Men in Black, and for a generation of hunters The Man had Fangs.<br /> <br /> [Picture: A canite hunter, base him on old photos of the Black Panthers, stands on top of a stone staircase, the kind you'll see outside government buildings or the Lincoln Memorial. He rests one foot on a staked vampire and has a circle drawn on his head (see the Canite in NS p153). He's currently in a Mexican stand-off against two police officers, holding one pistol in each hand, the Canite symbol floats behind each gun.]<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Rite of Denial: Antiquate</span></b><br /> <br /> The Canite writes a list of the Vampire\u2019s crimes, real or imagined, on a sheet of paper using blood for ink. Then, tucking the paper under his tongue he insults the Vampire. If the Vampire hears the insult, including through technological or supernatural means, the Rite takes effect.<br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Willpower, 3 thimbles.<br /> <b>Action:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Roll Results</b><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><b>Dramatic Failure:</b> The Canite fills their mind with memories of Canites from antiquity, they cannot hold more than flashes and suffer a Breaking Point.<br /> <b>Failure: </b>Nothing happens<br /> <b>Success:</b> The Vampire\u2019s mind is filled with the fog of ages. They forget everything they have learned to adapt since their mortal life. Any attempt to use Allies, Contacts, Mentor, Retainer, Staff, Status, or similar merits which represent ties to modern thinking people have their Successes reduced by the Canite\u2019s dots in Rites of Denial. Negative successes automatically become a Dramatic Failure. If using the Merit does not require a roll, and does require interacting with other people, the Storyteller should come up with a roll.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success: </b>As above, but the Canite\u2019s dots in Rites of Denial are treated as one dot higher.</div><i>&quot;Well that was a waste of time.&quot; said The Amazing Randi. &quot;I learned those tricks on the back of a cereal packet&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;So many new phenomena, so many hypothesis to test, and none of them were real.&quot; replied Professor Gordon.<br /> <br /> The third member of the group made a choking sound as she struggled to speak, but the others heard her voice in their minds clearly. &quot;It was nice to get out for a bit&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're sounding better.&quot; said Randi. &quot;I think the new meds are working. With a few more tests I think you'll have an independent life.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes&quot; said Gordon. &quot;Enough of this nonsense, let's get back to proper science&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-07-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T11:47:27-07:00","id":582571,"title":"","content":"So a while back there was discussion of an ambitious project. A series of Hunter Dark Eras stretching from the almost modern back to ancient Judea. It didn't get far, but I did post one small part of Countercultural Hunter, and I thought I may as well finish off. I don't really think there's much I can talk about here that I didn't mention in the opening section. It was very nice to do a little something with the Athenic Church again. (BTW, the most up to date version of them is <a href=\"http://hunter-the-vigil-cults.wikia.com/wiki/Hunter_the_Vigil:_Cults_Wiki\" target=\"_blank\">in the Cults wikia</a>).<br /> <br /> One thing you'll notice is how heavily this ties into WWII. I proposed that we write the eras in reverse so each Era could link back to the one before it. I still think that's a neat idea, and I would love to do WWII Hunter at some point. IMO it redefined the Vigil; especially if you include some of the fan groups: MI18, KSI, Order of St. Anthony, Soci\u00e9t\u00e9 d\u2019Had\u00e8s, Hakollel shel Hamerkava - they all trace their origin (or present status for the Order) to WWII. Between showing what the Vigil is like in war torn nations, what the vigil is like on the front lines, and the historical significance... one day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Oh, and the Amazing Randi is talking about Uri Geller. He and two other members of Null Mysteriis (Randi is obviously NM) just finished debunking him. It was easy since one of the three can just read Uri's mind.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 07-11-2015, 04:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T06:30:43-07:00","id":583431,"title":"","content":"It reminds me a lot about <a href=\"http://massivelyop.com/2015/07/01/the-secret-world-developers-look-forward-to-the-games-third-anniversary/\" target=\"_blank\">latest Secret World event</a> about Hippies and Guardians of Gaia. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://massivelyop.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/07/tsw-development-epl-701-860x280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://massivelyop.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/06/Untitled1-860x280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:57:26-07:00","id":584879,"title":"","content":"I preper to play in 60s <b>Hunter</b> in mine's buddy game, so this material is golden for us. I only need one more thing to the puzzle - <b>Did counterculture was not opposed to mainstream?</b> Did not most of American society being run like in second seson of <i><b>American Horror Story</b></i>, called <i><b>Asylum</b></i>? Hippies did not fighted with police and structues points of power? If all those are yes, did not this mean that Hippies Hunters would not fight with Mainstream Hunters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T14:52:09-07:00","id":585243,"title":"","content":"While Hippies did conflict with mainstream society. I imagine mainstream Hunters and Hippy Hunters would mostly ignore each other.<br /> <br /> Most Hippy Hunters were doing weird stuff like using drugs to explore the Astral Realms or moving away and living in remote communes. Mainstream hunters probably wouldn't even notice hippy hunters - unless their mundane life comes into conflict with the hippy's mainstream life.<br /> <br /> Of course this doesn't last. At some point one of the Conspiracies notices the hippies, spies on them until they have enough information, and crushes the hippy hunters utterly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:04:26-07:00","id":585266,"title":"","content":"is there going to be a special Era compact- like a compact of hippie shaman hunters? I mean, yeah, I know that the Maiden's Blood and the Athenic Church are the survivors, and the Guardians of the Source are (controversial) hippie hunters while the Illuminated Brotherhood are drug using spirit mediums, but I'm asking nicely <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:52:02-07:00","id":585304,"title":"","content":"I have no particular plans to write up any Compacts from this era at the moment. I've got lots of, I wouldn't call them concepts or ideas, but I know how the groups would form. But if I wrote them up I can't think of anything they'd say that isn't mostly in the first post. Where's Glamourweaver when you need him?<br /> <br /> <br /> The Hippies would have two main compacts: The spirit scapers and the psychonaughts; the two groups would be strong allies with some dual memberships and shared communes. The Psychonaughts would mostly be attempting to explore the Astral, the Shadow, and have less reliable ways to perceive some other realities like ghosts in Twilight. The spirit scapers would mostly stick to basic proven techniques to see the Shadow. Ignoring the riskier experimental drugs that let you explore the Shadow or do anything with other realms in favour of a somewhat safe Two World Eyes.<br /> <br /> Also note that the Illuminated Brotherhood was formed from an attempt to recreate the Marsh Chapel experiment, which took place in 1962. Its almost certain that the psychonaughts were aware of this experiment. It's possible that whoever's responsible for the Illuminated Brotherhood might have been trying to retrace the steps of the psychonaughts and rediscover their techniques. Marsh Chapel would be one of the clues not locked away in some Conspiracy's archive.<br /> <br /> <br /> Feminist Hunters would typically advance from Cell to Compact when they discover something that can provide an actual ideology for a Compact. The Hippy goal of forsaking the modern world for a simpler and more spiritual life has a built in place for Hunters who get genuine Spirtuality. The feminist goal of changing society doesn't really have much room for occult specalists since the occult is more dangerous and unless you're really really good or a major template, less effective than activism.<br /> <br /> However the odds of finding something that you can build a Compacts ideology around; and that something being comparable with your own ideology is pretty low. Just look at the examples - the Sisterhood believe in defending mortals from supernatural predators - mostly tangential to feminism. The Athenic Church call themselves feminists,<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Medusa\" target=\"_blank\"> but read some classical mythology about Athena</a>. There'd be one or two genuinely feminist Compacts, but between Hunters being sucked off into non-feminist Compacts on one side and Hunters giving up the Vigil to go back to regular feminism on the other side; there wouldn't be many.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally the Civil Rights movement. Hippy and Feminism is new territory full of unaligned hunters looking to climb the Tiers. Defending African Americans is old territory and solidly Cainite territory. Any time a Cell of hunters in the Civil Rights movement reaches the point where it starts recruiting and attempts grow into a Compact; the Cainites will hear. They'll turn up with the recruitment pitch and the promise of blood magic. Either the new guys end up Cainites. Or they've said no to a Conspiracy of fanatics who're starting to wonder what motives turned them away from the light. Are they perhaps being manipulated by vampires? And of course, you have Klansmen, police and other mortal threats against African American groups arming up.<br /> <br /> So IMO it's either Cell or Cainite in the civil rights movement. Not one Civil Rights Compact managed to form. You might get other Compacts or Conspiracies recruiting from the African American population but unlike the Canites they aren't actually part of the Civil Rights Movement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/582548-micro-dark-era-counter-cultural-usa?p=585266#post585266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guardians of the Source are (controversial) hippie hunters</div> </div> </div> </div> Who are they? I think I'd remember a cannon Hippy Hunter group <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously. The spirit scapers are what the Guardians of the Source should have been. Shaping the Hisil gives them an actual reason to fight over lay lines that doesn't make them wrong about everything. If you want to make them vicious bombers then sure; somebody's got to protect the commune from Werewolves that think the Herd has no right messing with the spirits","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-21-2015, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T17:47:12-07:00","id":585482,"title":"","content":"I think a little sidebar or small compact of the New Earth Army would be a cool addition to this micro-dark era esp if this era extends into the 70's and 80's","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T00:37:40-07:00","id":585730,"title":"","content":"Write one up <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for when the era ends. In my non-historians opinion, it peaked at 1968. By 1973 it's practically over, and I'd say even the die hards get the picture in 1976.<br /> <br /> <br /> IMO the era starts ending around late 67, early 68 with the passing of the Civil Rights Act and COINTELPRO leading to the Canites loosing their connection to mortal activists.<br /> <br /> There were 26 race riots in the 6 years 1962-1968 and 23 in the 46 years 1969-2015 showing an increasing distance between the Canites violent activism and regular African American society while the FBI's COINTELPRO moves against the Black Panthers encouraging the Canites to lower their profile.<br /> <br /> <br /> The feminist vigil officially ended in 1976 when the publication of When God Was a Woman; but that's just a convenient marker point. The only reason a book published by mortals could end anything was because the whole feminist Vigil had been winding down for years. You can already see public Dianic Wiccian coverns in 1971 which shows a refocusing on mortal society rather than genuine occult. By 1976 the only feminist hunters would be people that essentially were both feminists and hunters instead of feminist hunters (e.g. The Maidens Blood Sisterhood.) When God Was a Woman just made them admit the truth. Groups like the Athenic Church never admitted it but since their &quot;Athenic feminism&quot; has no social ties to regular feminism they don't count.<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally the hippies would peek around 1969 around Woodstock. Their end comes very suddenly since the Conspiracies take them out in one fell swoop, rather than the Canites more gradual departure and the feminist groups being absorbed, destroyed, rebranding or disbanding one by one. By 1972 the last vestiges of the hippy vigil are isolated communes with little influence or visibility on the wider world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 08-27-2015, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T02:00:09-07:00","id":585776,"title":"","content":"Connecting the Counter Culture Dark Era, what do you think about <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stonewall_riots\" target=\"_blank\">Stonewall Riots</a> repercussions and LGBTQ Rights movement born? It's Civil Rights, all the way. I even seen connections of Race Rights and LGBTQ Rights movements document. Would not been reflected somewhere in the Hunters society of Era?<br /> <br /> I would also gladly hear about Carthian Movement, Iron Masters, Free Council's and Spring Court's interactions with Counter Culture Hunters of this Dark Era, especially as they are most probable to interact with Hippies-like groups. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 07-10-2015, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T04:24:05-07:00","id":585846,"title":"","content":"Stonewall has nothing to do with hunters. Since LGBT can be invisible in a way racial minorities can't be you won't see vampire's targeting them extensively until after they from a visible community - and in the 60s that's a very recent occurrence. Thus the historical factors that tied the Civil Rights movement into the Vigil don't apply.<br /> <br /> Carthian Movement - monsters who prey on and corrupt idealistic activists. Most Carthians spend the time growing in power and influence, until they're suddenly staked by the Canites.<br /> Iron Masters - no Tribe wide opinion. Probably mortals to themselves, until they realise they're mucking around with Spirits.<br /> Free Council - Don't exist in my WoD; but have a look at VALKARIE's section again <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Spring Court - Which freehold are you asking about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T11:34:20-07:00","id":586295,"title":"","content":"Okay Quick first pass, after looking into some background and trying to fit the concept within the timeline you have<br /> <br /> The Easlen Humans: (Compact)<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">Mother Earth, you're my life support system. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">As a soldier I must drink your blue water, live inside your red clay and eat your green skin. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">Help me to balance myself. As you hold in balance, the Earth, the sea, and the space environments. T</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">Help me to open my heart, knowing that the Universe will feed me. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">I pray my boots will always kiss your face, and my footsteps match your heartbeat. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">Carry my body through space and time. You're my connection to the Universe and all that comes after. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">I'm yours and you are mine. I salute you.</span></span></i></div><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Verdana, Arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#333333\">The Easlen Humans (who are renamed in 1979 to be the One Earth Battalion) are a compact of hunters that sprung out of the combined mindset of martial arts practitioners, Human Potential, and Non-violent retaliation. The principles of non-violence were understood to add no violence to any situation but to manipulate the violence that others bring away from the innocent and on to the creators of the violence, as violence always begets violence and harms the initiator (usually after it harms many others) The Easlen's Understood the best recourse was to cut out the middle-men and any other victims than the perpetrator of the violence from the way of harm. they generally follow the Ethos of the &quot;Warrior Monk&quot;, Testing the limits of their potential with a mix of meditation, sparring, and heavy psychedelic use to push the boundaries of their consciousness. As part of the ethos of Human Potential, The Easlen's will work to undo or mitigate supernatural influence on humanity, while treating supernatural monsters as the humans and consciousnesses that they understand them to be.<br /> <br /> Origins: The Easlen Humans trace their start to a meeting between Alan Watts, a British philosopher who studied Eastern religion and Dick Price, a former member of the air force who had suffered a Psychotic Break in 1956 on an air force base in the East Bay, which led to his hospitalization and discharge (further research using distant perception and psychedelic drugs show that this break was caused by Paradox, however, That was far after the formation of the new earth army and a segment of its installation in the United states Armed Forces thanks to the work by Jim Channon) Price met with a friend Michel Murphy and Using some of the techniques Murphy learned in india about unlocking the full potential of the brain, convinced Murphy's Grandmother to lease them the familys property in Big Sur. There they created the Easlen Institute Headquarters for the Easlen Humans. It is in this institute that classes are run by members of the Compact, including Adolus Huxley, Hunter S. Thompson, Gia-Fu Feng, And others.<br /> <br /> <b>Status/Mystery Cult Initation: Easlen Institute </b><br /> * The Student trains their body and mind heavily, they gain the Meditative Mind merit at 1 dot<br /> ** The Student begins to train their body in the methods of non-violent resistance, They gain the Defensive Combat merit for brawl (NOTE if playing with the First Earth Army Battalion, this can be used for Weaponry instead)<br /> *** The student has begun to unlock the potential of their body by linking it to the mind and spirit, They gain Biokenisis **<br /> **** The Student has begun to understand the true interconnectedness of all things. They gain the Clairvoyance Merit.<br /> *****The Student has mastered their body and mind, and are a fully realized warrior monk. When Involved in Down and Dirty Combat, the Master can take the Guilty condition (s they accept the repercussions for their actions) to gain a +4 bonus to their Down and Dirty Dice-pool. </span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5718,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","user":"Hackthulhu","date":".  edited starting date to be correct 07-13-2015, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T14:31:33-07:00","id":586444,"title":"","content":"As to Free Council. you mean this paragraph?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/582548-micro-dark-era-counter-cultural-usa#post582548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two decades before the summer of love Task Force: VALKYRIE had a problem, that problem was communism, and also Witches. The Task Force's increasing competence at getting information about Witches had unearthed a recent and growing vein of socialism. To say the Men in Black were terrified would be putting it mildly but between their regular monster hunting duties and Ivan VALKYRIE just didn't have the resources to open a third front, and so they made a Faustian bargain that still haunts them them to this day. They funded vampires to fight a proxy war against the witches.<br /> <br /> But to get the full story you must go back even earlier, to America's shameful history of slavery. Vampires are timeless creatures, and rather predictable in their way. They need blood, and slaves were an almost limitless supply. In turn the Cainite Heresy, who only see race as \u201chuman, vampire and everyone else\u201d, did as they always had done and recruited the vampire's victims, slaves and abolitionists alike.<br /> <br /> In the 1960s these two stories combined in a perfect storm that would define a generation of the American Vigil.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the VALKYRIE was twice as much obssesed with comunist witches in the Free Council? What about Neo-Liberal ones? <br /> <br /> And did I see it right - VALKYRIE has putted witches on the vampires, so the monsters would kill themselves out? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sping Court - We will start the game in the Lousiana, so maybe those. To contrast, maybe write about California nad New Yorks also? And, if I remember correctly, <i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Bodhisattvas of the </span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Broken Cage Entitelment</i> is coming directly from the Counter Culture of this Dark Era.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T03:54:57-07:00","id":588005,"title":"","content":"Good start on the The Easlen Humans; but I can't help notice they're founded in the 90s. Is that a typo?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/582548-micro-dark-era-counter-cultural-usa?p=586444#post586444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the VALKYRIE was twice as much obssesed with comunist witches in the Free Council? What about Neo-Liberal ones?</div> </div> </div> </div> This is McCarthy era, so pretty focused on commies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/582548-micro-dark-era-counter-cultural-usa?p=586444#post586444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And did I see it right - VALKYRIE has putted witches on 